-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  lex_identifiers_err_char_utf8.pcpp - Lexical: a non-ASCII character

  Break step of lex_identifiers: a character outside ASCII starts no token
  where an identifier or operator could start, so the euro sign is one
  LX0004 for all three of its bytes. The string before it holds a two-byte
  character: the column is a byte column (clang's unit), so the euro sign's
  column counts both bytes of that e-acute.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe lex_identifiers_err_char_utf8;

/*
  @@test
    kind error
  @@end
*/

begin
  println("é"); € // ERROR LX0004@17: Invalid character in source
end.
